Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:32:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] check this setup: a picture counts from when it comes up over
 the whole screen

A test picture was stopped when the full-screen video was not up 2
seconds after Kodi began to play it (to catch Back, which leaves the
picture playing behind the menu). Kodi brings up the full-screen video
only once the streams of the clip are ready (VideoPlayer,
SignalStreamsReady()), after the change of mode and of the HDR signal
that the clip asks for, so a start that takes longer than that cut the
clip before it was ever seen: on the forum of LibreELEC (2026-11-20) the
HLG card, the only clip at 50 Hz, showed only the dimmed menu and its
question.

A picture now counts from when it came up over the whole screen: Back is
what takes it away once it was up, its length and the 10 seconds past it
are counted from then, and a picture that has not come up 30 seconds
after it began to play (SHOW_LIMIT) is stopped. A clip in a window (the
sounds) counts from its start, as before. Where a picture never came up
while it played, the result says so (33674, in English and the three
Spanish ones), since the answer may not be of it. Why each clip stopped,
and when it came up, go into kodi.log and into the summary of the
results (clip_stop=end|back|not-shown|limit|check|not-started,
clip_shown=, clip_played=), so that a report shows it. At its end, Kodi
closes the full screen as the player stops; that is counted as the end,
not as Back.

Host tests (fake Kodi of the tests of this check): a picture that comes
up after 6 s plays to its end; one that never comes up is stopped at 30
s and the result says so; one that ends before it came up says so; Back
once it is up stops it at once; the string is in the four languages.
The five fail on the code of 1.1 and pass with this. The other tests of
the check give the same results with and without it.
